BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:STEFF: Island of People (Pongso no Tao)
DTSTART:20260418T223000Z
DTEND:20260419T001500Z
DTSTAMP:20260418T223000Z
UID:RyoUwWFvrv
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 89 mins (1h29m)\n\nPresented by GreenShower Collect
 ive Celebrate the historic launch of the 1st Seattle Taiwanese Eco Film F
 estival (STEFF)\, hosted by GreenShower. For the first time\, we are bring
 ing a curated selection of award-winning Taiwanese environmental cinema to
  the United States. This double-feature event explores our delicate bond w
 ith nature: from the investigative journey of Birds and Us to the poignant
  cultural struggle on Orchid Island in Island of People (Pongso no Tao). T
 hese films unveil the hidden environmental and social challenges facing Ta
 iwan’s ecosystems and Indigenous traditions. Join us for this landmark c
 ultural exchange\, featuring an exclusive live remote Q&A session.\n\nhttp
 s://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/1st-seattle-taiwanese-eco-film-festiva
 l-pongso-no-taoisland-of-people\n\nEstimated start: 15:45
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summer Wars (2009)
DTSTART:20260418T223000Z
DTEND:20260419T005000Z
DTSTAMP:20260418T223000Z
UID:Mxgkc5jGL9
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 124 mins (2h04m)\n\nKenji is a teenage math prodigy 
 working for OZ\, who is recruited by his secret crush Natsuki for the ulti
 mate summer job – her fake boyfriend... until a rogue A.I. program steal
 s his online identity\, and Kenji is accused of hacking OZ and causing rea
 l world catastrophes.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/ani-mara
 thon/summer-wars\n\nEstimated start: 15:45
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
